      "query": "{\"content\": \"The Supreme Court is very likely to deny review in *Ortiz-Col\\u00f3n v. United States*, with only a 4% chance of granting the petition. After being convicted in Puerto Rico of both enticing minors online and producing child pornography, Francisco Ortiz-Col\\u00f3n argued under the Constitution's Double Jeopardy Clause\\u2014which forbids punishing a person twice for the same crime\\u2014that those two charges overlapped. Although the Court asked the federal government to file a respons",
